  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "A laptop's battery life on a single charge is normally distributed with an average of $8$ hours and an unknown standard deviation. Tests show that $20%$ of laptops die after $11$ hours of usage. Assuming a normal model, what percentage of laptops will last less than $6$ hours on a single charge? **Round the answer to $1$ decimal place.**\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.75$ | $0.8$ | $0.85$ | $0.9$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |\n\n*In addition, you're given the following table of values for $p=\u03a6(z).$*\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.2236\\,$ | $\\,0.2206\\,$ | $\\,0.2177\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.2546\\,$ | $\\,0.2514\\,$ | $\\,0.2483\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.2877\\,$ | $\\,0.2843\\,$ | $\\,0.2810\\,$ |\n\nApproximately\n{{field-1}}$%$ of laptops will last less than $6$ hours on a single charge.",
